    {
      "id": "es-child",
      "title": "Children 8–12 (already reading and writing in their first language)",
      "learner": "Children aged 8–12 who read and write confidently in English (or another first language); 2–3 lessons a week of 40–50 minutes; school or after-school setting",
      "goal": "Reach a solid A1 and a partial A2: talk about themselves, family, school, likes and daily life, tell what they did, and read and write short texts",
      "entry": "Start from sounds, letters and greetings (no grammar needed), then build vocabulary around the child's own world before verbs; songs, games and pictures carry the grammar as chunks first",
      "assumes": null,
      "adapt": "Little grammar terminology; mastery checks favour match, listen-comprehend, role-play and short written production. Adult topics (work, money, politics, formal emails, telephone services) and abstract A2 items (certainty scales, por/para, perfect vs preterite variation, mediation) are left out; they can be added when the learner moves on. Tú forms dominate; usted is recognised.",
