    {
      "id": "es-adult-travel",
      "title": "Adults: everyday life and travel",
      "learner": "Adults with limited time (1–3 hours a week) who want to travel, live temporarily or socialise in a Spanish-speaking country; prefer practical phrases over grammar study",
      "goal": "Handle travel and everyday transactions early (ordering, buying, getting around), then talk about themselves and their experiences and solve common problems (health, phone, services)",
      "entry": "Starts with greetings and the survival units (food, shopping, transport) so that learners can use Spanish on a trip within weeks; prerequisites such as numbers and articles are pulled in automatically",
      "assumes": null,
      "adapt": "Usted and tú both practised from the start; the learner's target region decides vocabulary (móvil/celular, coger/tomar) and past-tense norm. Classroom vocabulary, -mente adverbs, gender exceptions, learning procedures and prepositional pronouns are left out (they can be picked up as needed); everything else follows. Mastery checks favour role-play and real-document-scan tasks.",
